  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The root cause of this event was that the operating ratio of the rupture disc was not used to develop effective operating limits to protect the integrity of the disc. The direct cause of the event was leakage through the 2-RPD-073-0729 inner rupture disc, due to exceeding its recommended operational ratio and the lower tolerance of the burst pressure, resulting in deformation of the rupture membrane and eventual failure.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "inadequate operating-limit basis for rupture disc",
    "provisional": true
  },
