  "notes": "Cause code TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields (no official cause code assigned). Root cause is procedural/engineering (operating limits not established for disc), consistent with a personnel/design-basis theme, but category is left provisional per authoritative fields. Discovery-to-failure chain spans ~2yr from Dec 2021 overpressure event to March 2024 rupture; treated as two distinct FailureMode nodes per rule 5 (damage vs. eventual rupture). Previous similar events section states no prior rupture disc failures at BFN in last three years -> no stub LER emitted since no specific prior LER is cited. RCIC/ADS backup only modeled for RCIC since narrative explicitly states RCIC remained operable; ADS/other ECCS mentioned only in general design-context/safety-analysis language ('all other ECCS and ADS valves were available... except during periods of planned inoperability') - treated as backup context but ambiguous scope, so only RCIC (explicitly operability-verified) is modeled as BACKED_UP_BY; Core Spray and LPCI are mentioned only in HPCI System Design context and excluded per rule 6."
